WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.150 --> 00:00:05.790
You would not force the people you love to do it your way.

2
00:00:05.790 --> 00:00:09.059
And about now, most people have an objection.

3
00:00:09.959 --> 00:00:12.719
That works in a marriage or a relationship.

4
00:00:12.719 --> 00:00:15.599
A country is millions of strangers.

5
00:00:15.599 --> 00:00:17.859
People act in their own interest.

6
00:00:17.859 --> 00:00:22.599
They game every system, and they behave worse when nobody is watching.

7
00:00:22.599 --> 00:00:23.759
Some steal.

8
00:00:23.759 --> 00:00:26.219
Some organize to do it for a living.

9
00:00:26.219 --> 00:00:29.298
Law and order is what makes a society function.

10
00:00:30.198 --> 00:00:33.738
Take that seriously, and test it against your own life.

11
00:00:33.738 --> 00:00:36.958
What is your greatest protection from other people?

12
00:00:36.958 --> 00:00:39.038
Most people answer fast.

13
00:00:39.038 --> 00:00:40.118
The police.

14
00:00:40.118 --> 00:00:40.759
The law.

15
00:00:41.659 --> 00:00:43.359
Now think about yesterday.

16
00:00:43.359 --> 00:00:47.239
The driver a few feet from you at seventy miles an hour.

17
00:00:47.239 --> 00:00:50.019
The stranger behind you at the cash machine.

18
00:00:50.019 --> 00:00:52.679
The neighbor who knows when you are away.

19
00:00:52.679 --> 00:00:56.279
Every one of them could have hurt you, or taken from you.

20
00:00:56.279 --> 00:00:59.199
No police officer was watching any of them.

21
00:00:59.199 --> 00:01:00.641
And nothing happened.

22
00:01:01.541 --> 00:01:03.701
What stopped them was not the law.

23
00:01:03.701 --> 00:01:06.121
It was something they carry with them.

24
00:01:06.121 --> 00:01:10.817
Your greatest protection from other people is the other people's values.

25
00:01:11.717 --> 00:01:13.417
The crime figures agree.

26
00:01:13.417 --> 00:01:19.437
In the United States in 2022, about a third of household thefts and break-ins were

27
00:01:19.437 --> 00:01:21.437
reported to the police at all.

28
00:01:21.437 --> 00:01:24.757
Of those, about one in eight was solved.

29
00:01:24.757 --> 00:01:27.777
That is roughly four in every hundred.

30
00:01:27.777 --> 00:01:32.007
Fear of arrest is not what keeps people out of your house.

31
00:01:32.907 --> 00:01:34.107
So what does?

32
00:01:34.107 --> 00:01:39.007
Start where the objection started: people act in their own interest.

33
00:01:39.007 --> 00:01:42.727
Everyone is after the same thing, a good life.

34
00:01:42.727 --> 00:01:46.667
And everyone has learned what violence and theft do to one.

35
00:01:46.667 --> 00:01:49.687
Being robbed never made anyone happier.

36
00:01:49.687 --> 00:01:52.727
Neither does living among people who cannot trust you.

37
00:01:52.727 --> 00:01:57.447
Most people work out early that they get further by dealing than by taking.

38
00:01:57.447 --> 00:01:59.207
That is not kindness.

39
00:01:59.207 --> 00:02:01.629
It is plain self-interest.

40
00:02:02.529 --> 00:02:04.409
But some people do steal.

41
00:02:04.409 --> 00:02:05.369
Yes.

42
00:02:05.369 --> 00:02:10.769
Some decide they are the exception: that what they want matters enough to take it.

43
00:02:10.769 --> 00:02:14.549
Organized crime is that decision turned into a business.

44
00:02:14.549 --> 00:02:17.809
And look at what it produces wherever it operates.

45
00:02:17.809 --> 00:02:18.749
Fear.

46
00:02:18.749 --> 00:02:20.129
Closed shops.

47
00:02:20.129 --> 00:02:24.809
People who stop trusting, stop building, stop dealing with each other.

48
00:02:24.809 --> 00:02:27.249
Crime does not refute the principle.

49
00:02:27.249 --> 00:02:28.469
It demonstrates it.

50
00:02:28.469 --> 00:02:34.529
Coercion, theft and violence always reduce happiness, harmony and prosperity.

51
00:02:34.529 --> 00:02:35.449
Always.

52
00:02:35.449 --> 00:02:38.269
And nothing here asks you to stand by.

53
00:02:38.269 --> 00:02:42.529
Someone who takes by force owes a debt to the person they took from.

54
00:02:42.529 --> 00:02:46.059
Stopping them, and making them repay it, is not in question.

55
00:02:46.959 --> 00:02:48.059
And law and order?

56
00:02:48.059 --> 00:02:50.079
Look at what it rests on.

57
00:02:50.079 --> 00:02:52.459
The law can deal with the exception.

58
00:02:52.459 --> 00:02:54.699
It cannot deal with everyone.

59
00:02:54.699 --> 00:02:58.899
It works because nearly everyone already holds the value.

60
00:02:58.899 --> 00:03:04.099
Order that rests on fear of punishment lasts as long as someone is watching.

61
00:03:04.099 --> 00:03:08.279
Order that rests on values holds when nobody is.

62
00:03:08.279 --> 00:03:10.261
Yesterday, nobody was.

63
00:03:11.161 --> 00:03:14.861
So look at where the objection started, and where it ends.

64
00:03:14.861 --> 00:03:19.721
It started with the harm done by people who take what they want by force.

65
00:03:19.721 --> 00:03:21.801
Nobody disputes stopping them.

66
00:03:21.801 --> 00:03:27.321
But it ends somewhere else: with force as the way a society gets things done.

67
00:03:27.321 --> 00:03:29.601
This problem matters enough.

68
00:03:29.601 --> 00:03:30.921
Make them pay.

69
00:03:30.921 --> 00:03:32.501
Make them comply.

70
00:03:32.501 --> 00:03:35.081
You would not take from your neighbor yourself.

71
00:03:35.081 --> 00:03:37.981
Would you ask another neighbor to do it for you?

72
00:03:37.981 --> 00:03:40.421
That is what a vote for force is.

73
00:03:40.421 --> 00:03:45.841
And if your protection is a value, what happens to that value in a society that

74
00:03:45.841 --> 00:03:48.627
practices its exception at every election?

75
00:03:49.527 --> 00:03:54.487
So carry the question this philosophy asks of anyone with a problem to solve.

76
00:03:54.487 --> 00:04:00.003
What kind of problem-solver or leader are you if no one is forced to do it your way?

77
00:04:00.903 --> 00:04:04.483
All of this leans on one claim: that coercion,

78
00:04:04.483 --> 00:04:09.523
theft and violence always reduce happiness, harmony and prosperity.

79
00:04:09.523 --> 00:04:10.823
Is that true?

80
00:04:10.823 --> 00:04:13.283
You can check it against your own life.

81
00:04:13.283 --> 00:04:17.283
That is next: What Flourishing Actually Means.

82
00:04:17.283 --> 00:04:21.435
The whole series, in order, is at humanrespect.app.
